<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Italian Wars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Italian Wars were a series of conflicts between 1494 and 1559 fought mainly between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, along with other powers, for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Spain emerged dominant, gaining control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. The wars helped establish the military reputation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> and its infantry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/italian-wars.jpg" alt="Italian Wars" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Waylon1104 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italian_War_Battle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
